Thomas Pornin wrote:
> According to Pieyed Piper  <TheBongShopAtTheEndOfTheUniverse>:
>
>>  Is the conical hat better or the helm?
>
> Usually, a helm of brilliance is better. But some Wizards may find the
> Cornuthaum (_not_ the dunce cap, which is also a "conical hat") a better
> choice than a helm of brilliance.

For wizard cornuthaum may be better at +0 but the difference reverses as
the enchantment goes up.  Brilliance gives 1 more AC point.  Cornuthaum
is one of the lightest of all items.  Weight makes a giant difference
for body armor, but not so much for helmet types.

I think for anyone other than a wizard the helm of brilliance is the
better choice.  It may be the best helmet type for any class but helmet
type is rarely crucial.  As the enchantment goes up two different
intrinsics follow, extremely nice.


